<article class="env-lemma" id="0GT5">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GT5">Lemma <span data-tag="0GT5">20.55.3</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0GT4" data-tag="0GT4">20.55.2</a> let $\mathcal{F}$ be an $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the subsheaf $\mathcal{F}[\mathcal{I}] \subset \mathcal{F}$ of sections annihilated by $\mathcal{I}$ is zero, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the subsheaf $\mathcal{F}[\mathcal{I}^ n]$ is zero for all $n \geq 1$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the multiplication map $\mathcal{I} \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ X} \mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}$ is injective, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every open $U \subset X$ such that $\mathcal{I}|_ U = \mathcal{O}_ U \cdot f$ for some $f \in \mathcal{I}(U)$ the map $f : \mathcal{F}|_ U \to \mathcal{F}|_ U$ is injective, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for every $x \in X$ and generator $f$ of the ideal $\mathcal{I}_ x \subset \mathcal{O}_{X, x}$ the element $f$ is a nonzerodivisor on the stalk $\mathcal{F}_ x$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
